  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which alpha-Cedrene epoxide may interact with SNB-78, through a series of molecular targets. The compound is directly linked to MOVP-3, which is a target of both Neridienone A and RXF 631. These compounds, in turn, are targets of SNB-78, indicating a complex network of interactions that ultimately lead to the inhibition of SNB-78. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with alpha-Cedrene epoxide acting as a central node in the pathway leading to SNB-78. The evidence supports a possible mode of action involving the inhibition of SNB-78 through the targeting of MOVP-3 and its downstream pathways. The integration of these findings implies that alpha-Cedrene epoxide may exert its effects by modulating the activity of SNB-78 through a series of molecular interactions, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism and therapeutic relevance.",
